# Build output.
/bin/

# Generated by `make generate`. Checked in by some templ projects and not by
# others; here it is not, because `make test` and `make build` both generate
# first, so a checkout can never be missing it for long.
*_templ.go
*_templ.txt

# Generated by `make css` from input.css, and regenerated whenever loom is
# upgraded. Not a source file.
/assets/css/loom.css

# assets/static/styles.css is NOT ignored, and the asymmetry is deliberate:
# it is embedded into the binary, so `go build ./...` fails outright when it
# is missing - and the scratch image has nowhere else to get it from. Keeping
# the compiled sheet in the tree is what lets a fresh clone run `go run
# ./cmd/deskline` before it has ever run `make css`.

# Attachments uploaded by the running app.
/tmp/
